OL,3,GNEWSA'Holy grail' long lost board game
OL,4,Afound in attic
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rare prototype of a board game -
OL,7,Fdescribed by a museum curator as a holy
OL,8,Fgrail - has been discovered in an attic
OL,9,Famidst a box of childhood toys.
OL,11,FStop or Go, a road safety game played
OL,12,Fon a grid with counters, was designed
OL,13,Fin the 1940s by the games company
OL,14,FPepys, but was never manufactured.
OL,16,FHeidi Gibbs found what is believed to
OL,17,Fbe a pre-production version of the game
OL,18,Famidst her late grandmother's
OL,19,Fbelongings and approached the Museum of
OL,20,FBoard Games in Newent in the Forest of
OL,21,FDean.
OL,23,APub: 07-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
